图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Outbound LLM request modification for DeepSeek Harness (DSH), at the fetch transport layer.","id":"gh:1335055853","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-custom-header","slug":"Asaiuta/dsh-custom-header","topics":["anthropic","claude-code","codex","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","fetch","header-injection","http","llm","middleware","opencode","plugin","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Outbound LLM request modification for DeepSeek Harness (DSH), at the fetch transport layer."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-custom-header"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Outbound LLM request modification for DeepSeek Harness (DSH), at the fetch transport layer.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"One `globalThis.fetch` middleware chain (keyed by a DSH-scoped symbol,\n`Symbol.for(\"dsh-custom-heade"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"r.fetch.pipeline.v1\")`) that every provider —\nwhatever plugin owns it — streams through:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **injects** client-identity headers (`User-Agent`, `Originator`,\n`X-Claude-Code-Session-Id`, `x-op"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"encode-*`, …) from presets that mirror real\nCodex / Claude Code / opencode clients\n- **strips** `X-S"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"tainless-*` runtime fingerprint headers\n- **rewrites** the request URL (path matching + `appendQuery"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"`)\n- **patches** request bodies: the Anthropic Messages identity / billing system\nblock + `metadata."},{"id":"p5s5","text":"user_id`, and the opencode Zen free-tier tool stubs"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> For servers you administer or are authorized to use. Cloudflare TLS/Bot\n> edge blocks need a diffe"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"rent API entry, an admin allowlist, or a local\n> forward proxy."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Why fetch, not a provider-owning adapter"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The 0.2/0.3 line rewrote this plugin as provider-owning `LlmAdapter`s\nregistered through `ctx.llm.re"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"gisterAdapter(routes, adapter)`. That extension\npoint is **per-route exclusive**: registering a rout"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"e another plugin already\nowns (say the `ziyong`/`moonshotai` providers that `llm-pi-ai` registers)\nt"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"hrows `DUPLICATE_ADAPTER`, and the host exposes no way to graft onto someone\nelse's adapter. The poi"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"nt of this plugin is exactly \"make requests to *my*\ngateway look like client X\" — whatever plugin th"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"ose requests come from — so it\nneeds a seat that owns no routes at all. The fetch layer is that seat"},{"id":"p8s7","text":": it\nintercepts the transport every adapter already uses."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The cost of the fetch seat is that only the request URL identifies a request\n(never the owning provi"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"der). So the `gatewayHosts` allowlist is the single safety\nboundary: **every profile — fixed ones in"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"cluded — touches only requests whose\nhost matches**, and an empty allowlist is a safe no-op."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`apply` registers four middlewares into the shared pipeline, each re-reading a\nsnapshot that `loader"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"/volatile-update` refreshes (a settings save therefore\nlands in the next request — no restart):"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| priority | middleware | what it does |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| 5 | `url-rewrite` | path matching + `appendQuery` / replacement, host-gated |\n| 6 | `header-strip`"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" | `X-Stainless-*` and runtime fingerprint removal, on profiles that ask for it |\n| 7 | `header-inje"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ct` | the resolved profile's identity headers + `extraHeaders` |\n| 8 | `body-patch` | Anthropic iden"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"tity body patch; opencode Zen `/zen` → `/inference` + `bash`/`read` tool stubs (free models only) |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The chain mechanics: an accessor `fetch` on `globalThis` whose setter keeps the\nunderlying fetch in "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"sync; middlewares compose on every (re)install, priority\nascending; each receives `{ input, init, ne"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"xt }` and may call `next` with\nrewritten input. The pipeline is vendored from\n`@aizigao/pi-fetch-pip"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"eline`\n(MIT), re-keyed for DSH so multiple plugins can coexist without clobbering each\nother's chain"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ine`\n(MIT), re-keyed for DSH so multiple plugins can coexist without clobbering each\nother's chains."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Session-scoped ids (`x-opencode-session`, `X-Claude-Code-Session-Id`,\n`metadata.user_id`) cannot be "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"read from a URL, so the plugin wraps the\n`llm/stream` waterfall: every adapter stream iteration — in"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"cluding the fetch it\nissues — runs inside an `AsyncLocalStorage` carrying\n`GenerateOptions.sessionId"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"`. That is what keeps concurrent DSH conversations\nfrom sharing one process-wide id. The same observ"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"er logs a 403 hint\ndistinguishing Cloudflare HTML edge blocks from JSON client-restriction\nrejection"},{"id":"p15s6","text":" logs a 403 hint\ndistinguishing Cloudflare HTML edge blocks from JSON client-restriction\nrejections."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Configuration is a schemastery `Config` schema on the plugin, validated by the\nLoader against `cordi"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"s.yml`. **Every field is `.volatile()`**, which is what\nmakes `dsh-settings` publish a writable name"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"space for the entry at all: its\n`describe()` collects only entries carrying a volatile field, and it"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"s writer\nrejects any other path. A volatile-only change is committed into the running\nfiber rather t"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"han remounting it — the host half re-reads its refs on\n`loader/volatile-update` instead of snapshott"},{"id":"p16s6","text":"g it — the host half re-reads its refs on\n`loader/volatile-update` instead of snapshotting at mount."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The page itself is the plugin's own browser half (`src/client/*`). It registers\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Profiles"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Each fixed profile is a complete client-identity header set:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Profile | Headers sent |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| `codex_desktop` | `codex_app/1.2026.0628 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64)` + `Originator: codex_app` "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"|\n| `codex_official` | `codex_cli_rs/0.147.0 (Windows 10.0.19045; x86_64) WindowsTerminal` + `Origin"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ator: codex_cli_rs` |\n| `codex_tui` | `codex-tui/0.147.0 (…; x86_64) WindowsTerminal` + `Originator:"},{"id":"p21s4","text":" codex-tui` |\n| `codex_claude_plugin` | `Claude Code/0.5.0 (Macos 15.5; arm64) iTerm2.app` + `Origin"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"ator: Claude Code` |\n| `pi_agent` | `pi-coding-agent/1.0` + `Originator: pi` (needs the server to ac"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"cept this identity too) |\n| `claude_code_messages` | `claude-cli/2.1.220 (external, sdk-cli)` + `X-C"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"laude-Code-Session-Id` + full `anthropic-beta` + body (`metadata.user_id` JSON / system block) |\n| `"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"opencode_zen` | `opencode/1.19.0 ai-sdk/...` UA + `x-opencode-client/project/session/session-id/requ"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"est` (descending `ses_` id) |\n| `auto` | on a matching host: Anthropic `/v1/messages` paths → Claude"},{"id":"p21s10","text":" set; anything else → `codexFallback` |\n| `off` | nothing |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"All profiles — fixed ones included — are gated by `gatewayHosts`. The Codex header\nvalues are verifi"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ed against openai/codex source (see \"Truthfulness\nverification\"); the opencode `Identifier` id schem"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"e (`msg_` ascending / `ses_`\ndescending, `hex12` + base62) and the Claude Code 2.1.220 header set ar"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"e\nre-implemented from their real-world formats."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Truthfulness verification (Codex presets)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Codex identity fields were checked against primary sources:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- **`Originator: codex_cli_rs`** — openai/codex\n`codex-rs/login/src/auth/default_client.rs`: `DEFAUL"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"T_ORIGINATOR = \"codex_cli_rs\"`.\n- **codex_official UA shape** — same file, `get_codex_user_agent()`:"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"\n`{originator}/{CARGO_PKG_VERSION} ({os_type} {os_version}; {arch}) {terminal}`,\nwith the terminal t"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"oken from `codex-rs/terminal-detection/src/lib.rs`\n(`WindowsTerminal` for Windows Terminal, `xterm-2"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"56color` from `TERM`, …).\nA literal `terminal` tail matches no real build and was replaced.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
